The crossing count is always zero, so no crossing is ever armed:
a thread whose deadline the running turn's reaches waits for the core's next macro tick,
not the moment between ticks the deadline crosses at.
The self-check's crossing equality still holds only while the count is the one the state gives.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work test qemu-replay
Report: a crossing is armed nearer than the switch it covers
Witness: fuzz lend-borrower-queued

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -1365,6 +1365,7 @@ static bool deadline_due(struct core *core)
  */
 uint32_t sched_crossing_counts_on(const struct core *core, uint32_t offset)
 {
+    return 0;
     if (core->turn == NULL || core->run_queue == 0) {
         return 0;
     }
